.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "ws: a Node\&.js WebSocket library"
.PP
\fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP

.PP
ws is a simple to use, blazing fast, and thoroughly tested WebSocket client and server implementation\&.

.PP
Passes the quite extensive Autobahn test suite: \fRserver\fP, \fRclient\fP\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP: This module does not work in the browser\&. The client in the docs is a reference to a backend with the role of a client in the WebSocket communication\&. Browser clients must use the native \fR\fRWebSocket\fP\fP object\&. To make the same code work seamlessly on Node\&.js and the browser, you can use one of the many wrappers available on npm, like \fRisomorphic-ws\fP\&.
